<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.5.4: Using Function Notation and Graphing Technology</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00925</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.5.4: Using Function Notation and Graphing Technology</md:title>
    <md:uuid>eb44e091-9498-4b0e-b2b5-85f7f3be5b7f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001">      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">The function <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>B</m:mi>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> is defined by the equation <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>B</m:mi>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mn>10</m:mn>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>25</m:mn>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>. Use the graphing tool here or
        technology outside the course. Graph the function.</para>
      <media alt="insert alt text">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media>
      <para id="para-00002">If needed, remember -</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>You can collapse the equation entry tab by selecting the button.</item>
        <item>To change the scale along either the x- or <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-axis, click on the wrench
          button and then enter minimum and maximum values for each axis and set the step value.</item>
        <item>To find a point on the line, click on the line and drag the mouse along the line to
          display the ordered pairs for each location.</item>
      </list>

      <!--Question
      1 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">What is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>B</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">


          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00005"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>B</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>85</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Question
      2 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">What were the window values you used for the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-axis? (Write the values
            as an inequality.)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">


          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00008"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Question
      3 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">What were the window values you used for the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-axis? (Write the values
            as an inequality.)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">


          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00011"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                <m:mn>100</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Question
      4 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00012">What is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>B</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2.75</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">


          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00014"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>B</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2.75</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>52.5</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Question
      5 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00015">What is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>B</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1.482</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">


          <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00017"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>B</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1.482</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>39.8</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Question
      6 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00018">What is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> if <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>B</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>93</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">


          <para id="para-00019">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00020"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>6.8</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Question
      7 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00021">What were the window values you used for the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-axis? (Write the values
            as an inequality.)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">


          <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00023"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                <m:mn>16</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Question
      8 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00008">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00024">What were the window values you used for the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-axis? (Write the values
            as an inequality.)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">


          <para id="para-00025">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00026"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>15</m:mn>
                <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                <m:mn>150</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Question
      9 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00009">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00027">What is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> if <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>B</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>42.1</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">


          <para id="para-00028">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00029"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1.71</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Question
      10 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00010">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00030">What is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> if <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>B</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>116.25</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">


          <para id="para-00031">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00032"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>9.125</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>

    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <exercise id="exer-00012">
        <problem id="prob-00012">
        <para id="para-00033"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_4_5_4_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>  
    </note>

    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>

      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title>Finding Missing Values</title>
        <para id="para-00035">Function <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>G</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> is defined by <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>G</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>20</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. Find the following values
          using graphing technology.</para>
        <para id="para-00045">a. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>G</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          </para>
        <para id="para-00036">To find <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>G</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>, look at <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> on the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-axis on the graph of <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>G</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. Use proper
          steps with your graphing technology to find the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-value on the line: <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>G</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>30</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.<media alt="Graph of a straight line with y-intercepts of 20 that passes through the point (2, 30).">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_08_11_01.jpg" width="300"/>
          </media></para>
        <para id="para-00046">b. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>G</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>32</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          </para>
        <para id="para-00037">To find the value of <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> where <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>G</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>32</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>, look at where the graph
          crosses the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-value of 32. Use proper steps
          with your graphing technology to find the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-value where the graph meets <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>32</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00038">
          <media alt="Graph of a straight line with y-intercepts of 20 that passes through the point (2.4, 32) a green horizontal line that passes through (0, 32).">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_08_11_02.jpg" width="300"/>
          </media>

        </para>
        <para id="para-00039"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>G</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2.4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>32</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Finding Missing Values</title>
      <para id="para-00040">Function <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>H</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> is defined by <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>H</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>. Find <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>H</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>10.4</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> using graphing
          technology.</para>
      <media alt="insert alt text">
            <iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/>
          </media>
        <exercise id="exer-00011">
            <problem id="prob-00011">
              <para id="para-00041">Use the graphing tool here or technology outside the course.
          Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00011">
              <para id="para-00042">Here is how to find the value of <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>H</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> using
          graphing technology:To find the value of <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> where <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>H</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>10.4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>, look at
          where the graph of <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>H</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> crosses the <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>-value of
          10.4. Use proper steps with your graphing technology to find the <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>-value where
          the graph meets <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>10.4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>.</para>
              <para id="para-00043"><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>H</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>3.2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>10.4</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00044">
                <media alt="Graph of a straight line with y-intercepts of 4 that passes through the point (3.2, 10.4) a red horizontal line that passes through (0, 10.4)">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_08_11_03.jpg"/>
                </media>

              </para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
    </section>

  </content>
</document>
